<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ărānĕōsus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		araneum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>full of spiders'
			webs</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">situs,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					25, 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>, <i>similar to
			cobwebs</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fila,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 19, 21, § 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caulis araneosus in mandendo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					21, 15, 51, § 87</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lanugo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 24, 12, 66, § 108 al.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
